<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Falkland Islands Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1851–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Falkland Islands Company is a British trading company incorporated by royal charter in 1851 to develop the Falkland Islands. It became the islands' largest landowner and employer, running sheep farms that exported wool to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, as well as shipping and the main stores in Stanley. Its dominance shaped the colony's economy for more than a century, until it sold most of its farmland in the late 20th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/falkland-islands-company.jpg" alt="Falkland Islands Company" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Apcbg · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Falkland-Islands-Company.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
